WEBVTT

1
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:45.875
In verses 13.6 and 13.7,

2
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:49.750
Lord Krishna describes the detailed
composition of the kshetra,

3
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.416
the body and the elements within it.

4
00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:54.291
This includes twenty-four elements

5
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:56.958
that make up the body and mind:

6
00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:59.125
the five great elements,

7
00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.125
the subtle elements of mind and intellect,

8
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:02.875
the senses,

9
00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:05.250
and the objects of the senses.

10
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.375
Lord Krishna also describes the
various transformations

11
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:11.416
and qualities that arise within the kshetra,

12
00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:15.250
such as desire, aversion, joy, and sorrow,

13
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.416
which shape the living being's

14
00:01:16.416 --> 00:01:19.041
experience of the material world.

15
00:01:19.041 --> 00:01:22.000
Understanding these components makes clear

16
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.666
the distinction between the kshetra, the body,

17
00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:27.708
and the kshetrajna,

18
00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:29.416
the knower of the body.

19
00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:34.000
And this very understanding leads
a person toward higher knowledge.

20
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:42.333
In verse 13.6, Lord Krishna presents

21
00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:44.333
the twenty-four elements

22
00:01:44.333 --> 00:01:47.291
that make up the kshetra.

23
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:53.041
The pancha mahabhuta, five great elements:

24
00:01:53.041 --> 00:01:53.833
earth,

25
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:57.083
water, fire, air, and space,

26
00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.791
which form the gross physical base of the body.

27
00:02:00.791 --> 00:02:04.458
Ahankara, the false ego:

28
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:07.708
the sense of false identity

29
00:02:07.708 --> 00:02:09.625
that causes a person to identify

30
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:11.541
with body and mind.

31
00:02:11.541 --> 00:02:13.916
Buddhi, the intellect:

32
00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:17.666
the power that distinguishes right from wrong

33
00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:21.041
and supports decision-making.

34
00:02:21.041 --> 00:02:23.500
Avyakta, the unmanifest:

35
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.208
also called prakriti

36
00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:26.125
or pradhana,

37
00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:29.541
the hidden state of the three gunas
of material nature,

38
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:34.416
sattva, rajas, and tamas.

39
00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:35.333
Lord Krishna then

40
00:02:35.333 --> 00:02:37.875
mentions the ten senses:

41
00:02:37.875 --> 00:02:39.250
Five jnanendriyas,

42
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.125
the senses of knowledge:

43
00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:46.500
eyes, ears, nose, tongue, and skin.

44
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.208
Five karmendriyas,

45
00:02:48.208 --> 00:02:51.458
the senses of action: speech, hands,

46
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:54.750
feet, the organ of elimination, and
the organ of generation.

47
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.708
To these, Lord Krishna adds
the mind as the eleventh sense,

48
00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:58.666
which coordinates and processes

49
00:02:58.666 --> 00:02:59.875
which coordinates and processes

50
00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:03.458
information received from the senses.

51
00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:04.416
Finally, He describes

52
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:06.250
the five sense objects,

53
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.541
the tanmatras,

54
00:03:08.541 --> 00:03:12.041
sound, touch, form, taste, and smell,

55
00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:13.333
which serve as stimuli

56
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:15.500
for the senses.

57
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.458
These twenty-four elements form
the framework of the kshetra,

58
00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:23.791
within which the jiva experiences life

59
00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:27.166
through the interaction of body,
mind, and senses.

60
00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:30.083
In verse 13.7, Lord Krishna turns to the vikara,

61
00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:35.000
the transformations that arise
within the kshetra

62
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.333
and shape the jiva's experiences:

63
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:42.041
It is included among the transformations
made by them,

64
00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:43.833
Iccha and dvesha - desire and aversion:

65
00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.583
impulses that attract or repel the mind

66
00:03:46.583 --> 00:03:49.583
toward various objects.

67
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:52.791
Sukha and duhkha, emotional responses

68
00:03:52.791 --> 00:03:57.791
arising from the fulfilment or
frustration of desire.

69
00:03:57.791 --> 00:04:01.166
Sangha, the aggregate:

70
00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:04.000
the physical body, composed of the
twenty-four elements,

71
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.833
which is the medium for experiencing
the material world.

72
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:08.875
Chetana, consciousness:

73
00:04:08.875 --> 00:04:11.666
though it originates from the soul,

74
00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:13.000
it becomes entangled in the kshetra

75
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.625
through its association

76
00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:16.791
with body and mind.

77
00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:20.916
Dhrti, steadfastness or resolve:

78
00:04:20.916 --> 00:04:23.500
the mental firmness that sustains efforts

79
00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.000
to fulfil desires or avoid suffering.

80
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.125
These transformations are like
the changing scenes

81
00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:30.625
of a film

82
00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:33.333
that hold the attention of the viewer.

83
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:34.791
Just as a person watching a film

84
00:04:34.791 --> 00:04:36.333
identifies with the emotions

85
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.000
shown on screen,

86
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.166
in the same way, the soul

87
00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:44.291
becomes absorbed in the experiences
of the kshetra

88
00:04:44.291 --> 00:04:48.041
and forgets its true identity.

89
00:04:48.041 --> 00:04:51.458
Understanding the field and its transformations.

90
00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:55.000
The kshetra passes through six
stages of transformation:

91
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.375
birth, growth, existence, reproduction,

92
00:04:58.375 --> 00:05:01.750
decay, and finally death.

93
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.416
As the body passes through these changes,

94
00:05:04.416 --> 00:05:05.875
the kshetrajna,

95
00:05:05.875 --> 00:05:07.208
the soul,

96
00:05:07.208 --> 00:05:10.250
remains unchanged.

97
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.791
But the soul, while bound,

98
00:05:11.791 --> 00:05:15.875
identifies with these changes,

99
00:05:15.875 --> 00:05:21.375
leading to attachment, joy, and suffering.

100
00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:24.583
A fitting example is a calf grazing

101
00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:26.291
within a fence.

102
00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.291
The calf can graze freely,

103
00:05:29.291 --> 00:05:32.833
but its field is limited by the fence.

104
00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:35.166
In the same way, the jiva's experiences

105
00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:38.125
are limited by the interactions of the
twenty-four elements,

106
00:05:38.125 --> 00:05:42.333
which set the boundaries of
material experience.

107
00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:45.375
Just as the calf, absorbed in grazing,

108
00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:48.625
remains unaware of the world beyond the fence,

109
00:05:48.625 --> 00:05:51.958
the soul, immersed in material life,

110
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:56.250
forgets its spiritual identity.

111
00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.041
The purpose of describing the kshetra -

112
00:05:59.041 --> 00:06:01.000
Lord Krishna's description of the kshetra
is not merely

113
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.958
for philosophical understanding.

114
00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:04.916
Its purpose

115
00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:08.291
is for Arjuna, and for us, to realise

116
00:06:08.291 --> 00:06:12.291
that the material body and its transformations
are temporary.

117
00:06:12.291 --> 00:06:16.000
True knowledge arises when
a person distinguishes

118
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.458
between the kshetra and the kshetrajna

119
00:06:18.458 --> 00:06:23.708
and recognises the Supreme
as the ultimate knower of all fields.

120
00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:26.666
In brief, verses six and seven

121
00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:27.875
the composition of the kshetra

122
00:06:27.875 --> 00:06:30.875
and its transformations describe in detail,

123
00:06:30.875 --> 00:06:32.833
through which a person can
develop detachment, 

124
00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:35.416
from the material body and on the soul,

125
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:40.333
and can focus on the Supreme's eternal reality.

126
00:06:44.625 --> 00:06:47.125
Have you ever said,

127
00:06:47.125 --> 00:06:49.625
'I am very angry'

128
00:06:49.625 --> 00:06:53.000
or 'I am very sad',

129
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:57.750
as if those feelings were your identity?

130
00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:01.541
Remember, they are not your identity.

131
00:07:01.541 --> 00:07:05.625
Your anger, your desire, your sorrow,

132
00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:06.958
these are not you.

133
00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:08.000
They are simply activities

134
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.375
within the field

135
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:13.250
of your body and mind,

136
00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.250
what I call the kshetra.

137
00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.375
You are the soul, the kshetrajna,

138
00:07:19.375 --> 00:07:22.125
the knower of the field,

139
00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:25.250
not the emotions themselves.

140
00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:29.833
Just as clouds pass through the sky

141
00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:34.916
without changing the sky itself,

142
00:07:34.916 --> 00:07:39.291
emotions pass through your mind

143
00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:42.500
without touching your true nature.

144
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:46.291
When you understand this,

145
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:51.583
you stop being overwhelmed.

146
00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:54.083
You can feel the emotion,

147
00:07:54.083 --> 00:07:57.166
but not be controlled by it.

148
00:07:57.166 --> 00:07:59.750
This knowledge is powerful.

149
00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.250
It helps you pause and choose

150
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.500
your response.

151
00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.916
You do not have to fight your emotions,

152
00:08:09.916 --> 00:08:15.500
nor do you have to become them.

153
00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.875
Stay aware of your true identity.

154
00:08:19.875 --> 00:08:23.375
And discover within yourself

155
00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:26.250
a calm, steady place

156
00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:30.500
that nothing can disturb.

157
00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:34.875
That is where true peace begins.

158
00:08:39.458 --> 00:08:41.416
In family life,

159
00:08:41.416 --> 00:08:43.500
many emotions keep coming and going,

160
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.541
Like - I want this,

161
00:08:45.541 --> 00:08:47.458
I cannot bear that,

162
00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:48.958
this made me happy,

163
00:08:48.958 --> 00:08:50.916
that caused me pain.

164
00:08:50.916 --> 00:08:52.750
These are natural.

165
00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.500
But

166
00:08:54.500 --> 00:09:00.541
when you fully identify with them,

167
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:03.083
they begin to control your behaviour

168
00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:07.416
with those you love.

169
00:09:07.416 --> 00:09:12.291
You fall under the sway of desire and aversion.

170
00:09:12.291 --> 00:09:16.333
And suddenly small issues

171
00:09:16.333 --> 00:09:19.083
become big conflicts.

172
00:09:19.083 --> 00:09:22.208
Joy and sorrow start deciding

173
00:09:22.208 --> 00:09:24.625
how you speak,

174
00:09:24.625 --> 00:09:26.375
how you behave,

175
00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:31.500
and even how much love you show.

176
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.250
But remember,

177
00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.833
these emotions are not you.

178
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:41.208
They are part of the field of body and mind.

179
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:43.375
You are the kshetrajna,

180
00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:44.666
the soul

181
00:09:44.666 --> 00:09:48.333
that observes and experiences them.

182
00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:51.458
When you understand this,

183
00:09:51.458 --> 00:09:54.416
you become calmer.

184
00:09:54.416 --> 00:09:57.916
You stop giving impulsive

185
00:09:57.916 --> 00:10:00.166
reactions.

186
00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:02.958
You learn to step back, reflect,

187
00:10:02.958 --> 00:10:06.625
and respond with greater wisdom.

188
00:10:06.625 --> 00:10:08.625
This awareness helps you become

189
00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:12.000
more balanced.

190
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.875
And when you are balanced,

191
00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:19.041
your family relationships naturally become

192
00:10:19.041 --> 00:10:23.500
deeper and more loving.

193
00:10:27.791 --> 00:10:30.416
In your professional life,

194
00:10:30.416 --> 00:10:34.250
every day you use your buddhi, mind,

195
00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.041
ahankara,

196
00:10:36.041 --> 00:10:39.125
and dhrti.

197
00:10:39.125 --> 00:10:42.208
These are valuable tools for success,

198
00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:44.875
but do not mistake them

199
00:10:44.875 --> 00:10:48.666
for your true self.

200
00:10:48.666 --> 00:10:51.666
You are not your position.

201
00:10:51.666 --> 00:10:54.708
You are not your role.

202
00:10:54.708 --> 00:11:00.125
You are not your wins, or even your failures.

203
00:11:00.125 --> 00:11:05.583
You are the kshetrajna behind all of these,

204
00:11:05.583 --> 00:11:07.041
the soul.

205
00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:09.416
When you forget this,

206
00:11:09.416 --> 00:11:13.291
work begins to grip you.

207
00:11:13.291 --> 00:11:16.291
Your emotions shift

208
00:11:16.291 --> 00:11:19.416
with every email or meeting.

209
00:11:19.416 --> 00:11:23.791
Your ego is hurt by criticism

210
00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:27.166
and inflated by praise.

211
00:11:27.166 --> 00:11:30.708
You begin to live as if your entire worth

212
00:11:30.708 --> 00:11:34.208
depends on your performance.

213
00:11:34.208 --> 00:11:37.000
That is when stress takes over

214
00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:41.000
and you become unbalanced.

215
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
But

216
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.000
when you remember,

217
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.958
'I am not these changing states,

218
00:11:50.958 --> 00:11:54.458
I am their witness',

219
00:11:54.458 --> 00:11:58.083
you regain control.

220
00:11:58.083 --> 00:12:01.791
You work better, think more clearly,

221
00:12:01.791 --> 00:12:04.875
and respond with greater maturity.

222
00:12:04.875 --> 00:12:07.791
So move forward,

223
00:12:07.791 --> 00:12:11.166
give your best in your work.

224
00:12:11.166 --> 00:12:15.833
Just do not lose yourself in it.

225
00:12:15.833 --> 00:12:21.000
Your worth goes beyond your work,

226
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:24.875
and it rests in

227
00:12:24.875 --> 00:12:26.958
who you truly are.
